        "white_belly"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "It has big, round ears, a bit like a mule's.",
      "tags": [
        "big_ears"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "diet",
      "text": "It is a grazer that mostly eats grass.",
      "tags": [
        "grazer"
      ],
      "source": "iucn"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It can go up to five days without drinking.",
      "tags": [
        "rarely_drinks"
      ],
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gr%C3%A9vy%27s_zebra"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "Males guard territories that hold water and good grass.",
      "tags": [
        "territorial"
      ],
      "source": "iucn"
    },
    {
      "category": "geography",
      "text": "Almost all of them live in northern Kenya, with a few in Ethiopia.",
      "source": "iucn"
    },
    {
      "category": "conservation",
      "text": "Loss of land, drought and poaching are its main threats.",
      "source": "iucn"
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "key_fact",
      "text": "It is the largest wild member of the horse family.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "key_fact",
      "text": "Foals are born with reddish-brown stripes that turn black as they grow.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "key_fact",
      "text": "Numbers fell from about 15,600 in the late 1970s to about 2,000 in 2004.",
      "source": "iucn"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "In Kenya, volunteers count them in a big photo census called the Great Grévy's Rally.",
      "source": "iucn"
    },
    {
      "category": "life_description",
      "text": "A mother carries her foal for about 13 months.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "threat",
      "text": "Grazing livestock compete with it for grass and water.",
      "source": "iucn"
    }
  ],
